.TH shutdown_now 2 2026-11-20 DarqOS "DarqOS Kernel API Manual"
.SH NAME
shutdown_now \- hurry a shutdown
.SH LIBRARY
.I darq
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BR shutdown_now ()
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR shutdown_now ()
hurries a running shutdown, or reboot: every process it's waiting for,
that hasn't said OK, is told ShutdownNow at once, and has its host
process killed 3 seconds later, if it hasn't exited.
Only a system process, one the p-kernel spawned, may: from any other,
it's ignored, and logged.
There's no response.
.SH ERRORS
None: a refusal is only logged.
.SH HISTORY
Introduced in \fISecond Edition\fP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
darq.shutdown_now()
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR on_shutdown (3),
